 "evidence": "A diagnostic on one model year at T21: an Earth-fitted sea-spray source function carried to lunar gravity by untested scalings (low, central and high cases), driven by 6.5-hour mean winds, and parcels followed on the lowest levels' winds with first-order removal. No measurement of spray at reduced gravity exists. The surf's spray and drops above 20 um of r80, which fall near the shore, are outside the source, and the model resolves no coast.",
 "reading_rule": "source gives the sea's yearly salt into the air under each law; the fate cases follow the central source, and their shares apply to any multiple of it. Chloride is 55% of the salt. chloride_kg_ha_yr and chloride_in_the_rain_mg_l are area-weighted over the model's land cells (lakes included); land_beside_the_sea are the model's land cells that hold part of the sea or touch a cell that does. salt_in_the_air_ug_m3 spreads the salt in the air over the mixed layer (1.7 km over water, 5 km over land). Multiply by the source cases' ratios to the central one for the low, high and gentle-law sources.",
